  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.dispatch_commitment and proxy.retention_commitment. commit_to_dispatch asks in the same order as before (forward body, prepare, signing window covers the completion bound, reserve, intent, record the crossing): the last three moved into dispatch_obligations::take, which keeps the order and the refusal at each step, and a refused reserve still commits no intent. DispatchedExchange::into_parts became split() returning the outcome and a PostDispatch (window, retention, intent) that the success exit takes whole. The signing-window bound now includes the commitment waits from other merged work (ADR-MCPRE-070 G1 and G2). EvidenceRetention's markers and writer moved into MarkerStage, RetentionQueue and WriterThread: the marker paths, the admission permit and the writer drain are the same lines, and the success exit's order (outcome committed, retention completed, then served) is held by the Committed and Retained types as before. The claim, premises and dependencies are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor, and every tested symbol the unit names still names a test function.",
